a: wait4 0 for TRACEME's own stop -> stopped SIGSTOP
a: PTRACE_CONT of the stopped child -> 0
a: wait4 WNOHANG at once, while the traced child runs -> 0 (none)
a: waitid WEXITED|WSTOPPED|WNOHANG while it runs -> 0, si_pid 0 (none)
a: wait4 WNOHANG every 10 ms until it stops -> stopped SIGUSR1
a: PTRACE_CONT suppressing SIGUSR1 -> 0
a: wait4 WNOHANG every 10 ms until it exits -> exited 7
a: wait4 WNOHANG once it is reaped -> -1 ECHILD
b0: wait4 0 for TRACEME's own stop -> stopped SIGSTOP
b0: a second thread's wait4 for the tracee's stop -> stopped SIGUSR1
b0: the second thread's PTRACE_PEEKUSER of the stopped tracee -> ESRCH
b0: the tracer thread's PTRACE_PEEKUSER of it -> a word
b-wall: wait4 0 for TRACEME's own stop -> stopped SIGSTOP
b-wall: a second thread's wait4 for the tracee's stop -> stopped SIGUSR1
b-wall: the second thread's PTRACE_PEEKUSER of the stopped tracee -> ESRCH
b-wall: the tracer thread's PTRACE_PEEKUSER of it -> a word
c: wait4 0 for TRACEME's own stop -> stopped SIGSTOP
c: poll of an empty pipe for 3 s while the tracee runs to its SIGUSR1 stop -> EINTR, SIGCHLD seen, before 2.5 s
c: then wait4 WNOHANG -> stopped SIGUSR1
d: wait4 0 for TRACEME's own stop -> stopped SIGSTOP
d: PTRACE_GETFPREGS -> 0
d: PTRACE_SETFPREGS of what GETFPREGS gave -> 0
e: PTRACE_SEIZE of a running child -> 0
e: PTRACE_INTERRUPT of it, running -> 0
e: wait4 __WALL after the interrupt -> stopped SIGTRAP event-stop
done -> ok
